<title>JAPAN: 110-120 yen/dlr no threat to Japan recovery - Utsumi.</title>
<headline>110-120 yen/dlr no threat to Japan recovery - Utsumi.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's economic recovery is not threatened as long as the dollar/yen rate remains between 110 and 120 yen, Makoto Utsumi, a former vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Asked about the effect of the yen's rapid rise on Japan's economy, Utsumi said that fluctuations had been sharp, but that, &quot;Between 110 and 120 (yen to the dollar), there is no problem (for Japan's economic recovery).&quot;</p>
<p>Utsumi spoke to reporters after a speech to an International Monetary Fund seminar.</p>
</text>
